*** Add File:runbooks/agent_governance_runbook.md
+# Agent Governance & Level-4 Activation Runbook
+
+Prereqs (must be satisfied before enabling AUTO):
+- HSM commissioned and dual-control activation completed (Vault PKCS#11 active).
+- Rekor restore drill passed and TLS cert lifecycle validated.
+- Vendor DPAs signed and private endpoints + BYOK configured for LLM vendors used by planner/verifier.
+- External pentest completed and critical/high findings remediated.
+- Governance Board approval with documented acceptance criteria and SLOs.
+
+Activation checklist:
+1. Set agent deployment control ConfigMap (ops/kill_switch/kill_switch_manual.yaml) to "PAUSED".
+2. Ensure OPA policies loaded into OPA (agent/opa/policies.rego).
+3. Deploy agent to staging (k8s/agent/agent-deployment.yaml) in SHADOW mode and run 10k shadow proposals.
+4. Run simulation adversarial tests in agent/simulator against representative scenarios.
+5. Validate verifier false-positive / false-negative rates are within thresholds.
+6. Sign-off: Governance Board approves promotion to AUTO in narrow domain (document domain & expiration).
+7. Enable AUTO via dual-control (Operator A creates a ticket; Operator B signs approval) and update ConfigMap to AUTO.
+8. Monitor initial 72-hour window under SRE and Security watch; have emergency rollback plan (set ConfigMap to PAUSED).
+
+Rollback & Kill-switch:
+- To immediately stop autonomous execution: kubectl -n ml patch configmap aegis-agent-control -p '{"data":{"mode":"PAUSED"}}'
+- To resume SHADOW: set to SHADOW (no executions).
+- Any mode change must be recorded in ticketing and evidence stored in MCP.
+
+Audit & Reporting:
+- The Agent records every proposal, decision, approval and action in MCP. Periodic reports (daily) are sent to Governance Board.
+
