+# Aegis Level-4 Autonomy Patch — What this adds (summary)
+
+This patch scaffolds a Level-4 agent runtime with:
+- Planner (LLM-based plan generation via existing LLM Adapter)
+- Safety Kernel (OPA policy + verifier integration)
+- Executor (action registry: k8s apply, Argo submit, Kafka, Vault sign placeholders)
+- Canary manager for automated promote/rollback flows
+- Simulator stub for shadow testing and digital twin runs
+- Agent API (submit goals, receive proposals, human decisions)
+- Configurable modes: SHADOW (default), AUTO (must be enabled via governance), PAUSED (kill-switch)
+- Evidence persistence to MCP for every proposal & decision (audit trail)
+- OPA policy example and runbook to coordinate governance board
+
+Important safety notes:
+- This is a high-assurance scaffold but does not by itself make autonomy safe—real safety requires HSM commissioning, Rekor drills, vendor DPAs/BYOK, external audits, and extensive shadow/simulations. Follow runbook before enabling AUTO.
